      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T07:53:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SOC_USBPD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT is used in upstream and cros_ec drivers:\nIn upstream (PR: https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/47015), we define SOC_USBPD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT default value 0 for gpio driver (disable unused cc pins and configure as gpio). \n\nIn cros_ec, if we enable ITE on chip pd module, we re-configure SOC_USBPD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT default value to 1.\nIn it8xxx2.c pd driver it8xxx2_tcpm_hook_connect/disconnect() according CONFIG_USB_PD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT value, we scan the port to set sleep mask (CONFIG_USB_PD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT \nvalue depends on SOC_USBPD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT).\n\nCONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_* is only defined in cros_ec and the prefix is not suit for upstream, so I rename it to SOC_USBPD_ITE_ACTIVE_PORT_COUNT.",
      "parentUuid": "56fdf8a1_0b4f0283",
      "revId": "eba34cd070820b20dd8576e6fe3cec9cdad1ff5f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c884a32c_b35197b8",
        "filename": "zephyr/Kconfig.tcpm",
        "patchSetId": 2
